    "zh": {
      "title": "品鉴《无人逝去》",
      "heading": "因为经常要靠听说书才能入睡\n不知不觉听了很多推理小说\n心血来潮就开始看一些推理小说了",
      "body": [
        "从此作开始正式入坑白井了",
        "五重反转 全员推理\n纯粹的 极高密度的伏线与逻辑推理\n从第一页开始提到的所有细节全都是伏线 平均十页一个推理\n没有社会派那些人性探讨 甚至也很少有人物和人物关系的塑造\n人物 设定 情节 包括动机\n一切都是为了诡计和推理服务",
        "真的太流畅 太爽了",
        "这就是设定系逻辑流吗\n这就是新本格吗\n这就是 白井智之 吗（仰望"
      ],
      "date": "2025.11.14"
    },
    "en": {
      "title": "Reading No One Died",
      "heading": "Book notes",
      "body": [
        "I often need an audiobook to fall asleep, and without noticing it I had listened to a great many mystery novels. On a whim, I finally started reading some mysteries for myself.",
        "This was the book that properly pulled me into Tomoyuki Shirai.",
        "Five reversals. Everyone reasons. It is pure, extremely dense foreshadowing and deduction. Every detail mentioned from the first page turns out to be a clue; there is practically a new piece of reasoning every ten pages. There is none of the social school’s examination of human nature, and barely any conventional shaping of characters or relationships. Character, setting, plot, even motive—everything exists to serve the trick and the deduction.",
        "It is unbelievably smooth. Unbelievably satisfying.",
        "So this is logic driven by an invented premise? This is the new orthodox? This is Tomoyuki Shirai? (looks upward)"
      ],
      "date": "14 Nov 2025"
    },
